{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass, when Pharaoh had sent — and did not lead.</b> He led them, as in ״לֵךְ נְחֵה אֶת הָעָם״ (Exodus 32), ״בְּהִתְהַלֶּכְךָ תַּנְחֶה אוֹתָךְ״ (Proverbs 6)." "<b>For it is near.</b> And easy to return by that road to Egypt; and there are many midrashic aggadot." "<b>Lest they see war.</b> Such as the war of ״וַיֵּרֶד הָעֲמָלֵקִי וְהַכְּנַעֲנִי וגוֹ׳״ (Numbers 14) — if they had gone a straight road they would have returned; and if when He made them go a roundabout way they said ״נִתְּנָה רֹאשׁ וְנָשׁוּבָה מִצְרָיְמָה״ (ibid.), had He led them on a direct route, all the more so!" "<b>Lest they reconsider.</b> They would devise a thought about having left, and set their hearts to return."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:00.325443350Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}